<title>BELGIUM: Euro Aluminium body declines comment on US talks.</title>
<headline>Euro Aluminium body declines comment on US talks.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Aluminium Association on Thursday declined comment on United States talks on abolishing a European Union tariff on aluminium mill product imports.</p>
<p>The U.S. Aluminum Association said it had held talks with the U.S. Trade Representative in Washington on Wednesday to press for the removal of the tariff.</p>
<p>&quot;I have no comment. Let's wait and see,&quot; EAA President Dick Dermer told Reuters.</p>
<p>U.S. and other world producers have for a long time challenged what they see as a trade-distorting tariff but EU producers say it provides protection against dollar fluctuations and cheap imports from east Europe.</p>
<p>In Duesseldorf earlier, the general secretary of the German aluminium industry association GDA said the talks were no cause for concern in Germany and were unlikely to bring action.</p>
<p>--Brussels Bureau +322 287 6830</p>
